  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Effective collaboration and partnerships between labour administrations, employers&apos; and workers&apos; organizations in order to achieve comprehensive responses for workplace compliance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The industrial relation space in Nigeria has face a lot of chalenges in recent mainly to the rising cost of living and negotiations for minimum wage. This has led to various industrial actions and strikes by different unions. The country has also witnessed a lot of court suits and summons over the years due to different breakdowns in negotiations and breach of agreements entered by the different parties - government, workers and employers. In order to address, the Federal Government of Nigeria is working on improving the industrial relations enviroment nad regulatory framework.

The ILO&apos;s interevntion will support the government and the socail partners to develop its first national Industrial Relations Policy (NIRP) that will provide the framework to regulate industrial relations practice in the country</narrative>
  </description>
